<title>UK: Euro jet gains with gas oil futures, but prems sli.</title>
<headline>Euro jet gains with gas oil futures, but prems sli.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>European jet fuel premiums were knocked lower on Wednesday by poor physical buying interest, but sharply stronger gas oil futures lifted prices.</p>
<p>April IPE gas oil settled $3.25 a tonne higher at $175.</p>
<p>A 2,000 tonne jet barge was heard bought at April IPE +$17 fob early, a dip of $1 on the premium, while cargoes were also seen to have slipped to about April IPE +$21 cif NWE.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 8980</p>
